    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">As the old saying goes, “All things prosper when the family is in harmony”. The socalled “family harmony” not only refers to the love between husband and wife, filial piety of children, brotherhood and friendship, but also refers to the fact that in case of conflict, family members will respect different opinions and tolerate each other. Such a “harmonious but different” family atmosphere can make each family member have a sense of belonging. Therefore, “harmony” is the core force to enhance family cohesion, which is particularly important for any family; especially for a large family like our Chua family, which has 13 siblings and 152 descendants.</marc:subfield>
